{"schema_version":1,"id":"june","title":"June 2026 calibration variants and chasing the origin","generated":"2026-10-30T18:07:33Z","generated_from":"gallery/data/export_ml.py","file":"ml/june.json","text":{"finding":"On the 906 IMPROVE filters the component count is set by the rule as much as by the data: CAL-0's curve gives k = 21 under 05's 2 % rule, 13 under 06's 5 % rule and 19 under 09's 10-fold CV, and 9 on 2nd-derivative spectra at about the same error. CAL-1's 3σ trim has the best in-sample R² (0.94) but a worse %RMSECV than keeping everything (143 % vs 98 %). Applied to the same 906 filters the candidate calibrations' median EC spans 10.7–13.5 µg. Against HIPS no change reaches slope 1 and intercept 0 together (at MAC 10): dropping the Teflon CF band keeps slope 1.03 at intercept -1.85, SNV reaches -0.33 at slope 0.65. The same 3σ rule removes 46–61 filters of 906 depending on K and when it stops (June 06's three rounds at k = 21 keep 860; spartan_ec 08's nine at K = 20 keep 845)."},"sources":[{"table":"rmsecv_curve","rows":30,"notebook":"05_calibration_variants","read":"tracked csv","path":"research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/tables/ec_rmsecv_curve.csv"},{"table":"rule_picks","rows":7,"notebook":"05_calibration_variants, 06_calibration_variants_components, 09_component_selection_fixed","read":"executed notebook output (printed)","path":"research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/05_calibration_variants.ipynb, research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/06_calibration_variants_components.ipynb, research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/09_component_selection_fixed.ipynb"},{"table":"variants","rows":8,"notebook":"06_calibration_variants_components, 09_component_selection_fixed, 10_calibration_variants_effect","read":"tracked csv","path":"research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/tables/calibration_variants_results.csv, research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/tables/component_selection_by_variant.csv, research/ftir_ec_calibration_2026_06_25/tables/component_selectio